  "notes": [
    "2M14503361+4921331, 2M15180013+0209292 and 2M19284379-0005176 are the last three rows of Tables 1-2 and are called unbound candidates in the captions (T:p4-b0, T:p5-b0; see also T:p6-b0). Their excess is only over MWPotential2014, within 1 sigma, and the paper later finds bound Irrgang Model I orbits and says they may be discarded as truly unbound (T:p6-b8, T:p11-b9); however, the abstract and summary retain the potential-dependent statement that three stars could be unbounded to MWPotential2014 (T:p1-b9, T:p15-b4). The separate appendix statement that 2M22242563-0438021 would become an unbound candidate under the StarHorse2 distance (T:p16-b11) is a distance-dependent aside, not one of the retained three candidates (T:p16-b12).",
    "2M14503361+4921331: Table 1's header reports α and δ as “deg ± mas”; the mixed units are preserved. The target appears among the last three rows of Tables 1–3, which the paper labels as unbound candidates with respect to MWPotential2014, but no numerical bound/unbound probability is tabulated for it, so no bound_probability or unbound_probability is included. No current galactocentric radius is tabulated for this star; Table 3 gives orbital peri/apogalacticon values, not the present-day galactocentric radius.",
    "2M15180013+0209292: The target 2M15180013+0209292 is one of the last three entries in Tables 1–3, described as an unbound candidate for MWPotential2014 but bound for the Irrgang Model I potential (e.g., T:p6-b0 and T:p15-b4). No numerical bound/unbound probability is tabulated for this star, so probabilities are not recorded. Table 1 lists α and δ in deg with their uncertainties in mas.",
    "2M19284379-0005176: Star 2M19284379-0005176 is one of the last three rows of Tables 1, 2 and 3, i.e., one of the three stars that exceed the escape velocity of the MWPotential2014 potential (unbound candidates per that potential only; Table 3 caption and Sect. 3.1/Fig. 1), while it remains bound in the Irrgang Model I and McMillan potentials and its excess over the MWPotential2014 escape speed is within the 1σ velocity uncertainties (Sect. 3.1, p6-b0). No per-star numerical bound/unbound probability is reported. The paper gives orbital parameters (R_peri, R_apo, e, Z_max, E) in Table 3, but no present-day Galactocentric radius value for this star, so galactocentric_radius is not recorded."
  ]
}
